  "notes": [
    "accept_source_upload: [SECURITY_BOUNDARY] MUST accept only the authenticated browser-owner context with valid same-origin and CSRF evidence, then pass the still-bounded stream to source custody; never treat a filename, media declaration, handoff identifier, or browser control as storage-path or authorization evidence.",
    "accept_source_upload_handler: [ORCHESTRATION] MUST read multipart UploadFile content incrementally under the 30 MiB limit, preserve only the safe display filename, verify the handoff secret without logging it, enforce CSRF before consumption, and delegate one module-owned concrete BinaryUpload adapter over the bounded UploadFile stream without buffering or interpreting the whole document; MUST NOT instantiate the BinaryUpload interface itself.",
    "issue_upload_handoff: [BEHAVIOR] MUST under one authorization decision, verify the exact Card, logical source, and expected current revision before issuing a new 900-second single-use handoff; persist only the verifier and return the bearer value once without placing it in Card data or logs; constructs the one-time SourceUploadHandoff value at the protected source-custody boundary.",
    "store_original_source: [PROVENANCE] MUST lock the exact handoff, identify an accepted content format from bounded bytes, stream to private candidate storage while calculating size and content hash, atomically commit immutable custody and consume the handoff, and make equal replay idempotent while rejecting conflicting bytes.",
    "retrieve_original_source: [SECURITY_BOUNDARY] MUST resolve only the authorized Card/source pair to its immutable verified content reference, reopen a private regular file beneath the configured store, recheck integrity, and return a module-owned concrete SourceDownload stream over that verified file with no filesystem path or credential; the module constructs SourceDownload; MUST NOT instantiate the SourceDownload interface itself.",
    "serve_source_download: [PATH_OR_ARTIFACT_POLICY] MUST return the concrete SourceDownload implementation obtained from source custody as a non-inline attachment source using an encoded safe display filename and verified media type, disable active-content interpretation, and never expose the internal storage reference in headers, body, logs, or errors; MUST NOT instantiate the SourceDownload interface itself.",
    "authenticate_request: [SECURITY_BOUNDARY] MUST accept only the bounded self-identifying bearer shape `<credential_id>.<secret_material>` emitted by enrollment or rotation, protect the complete bearer with the configured pepper, and use `CabinetUnitOfWorkFactory.open`, `begin`, `lock_abuse_context`, `load_throttle_state`, `load_credential`, `load_principal`, `update_credential`, `upsert_throttle_state`, and `insert_security_audit` inside one commit-or-rollback transaction. It MUST select exactly one verifier by parsed credential identity and exact channel, apply indistinguishable failure handling and the configured abuse throttle, compare the protected verifier timing-safely, return only an active principal of the expected kind, and never retain or persist the presented bearer.",
    "authorize_capability: [BEHAVIOR] MUST open one operation UoW, re-read the exact principal with `load_principal`, derive one deterministic scope key from the complete typed `EntityScope`, and call `load_capability_grant` for the exact principal/channel/capability/scope identity before committing secret-free audit evidence. It MUST re-evaluate current lifecycle state and the exact closed pair declared by = rules.capability_catalogue.grantable on every call, return a scoped decision only for the matching persisted grant, and otherwise roll back and raise AuthorizationDeniedError without prefix, suffix, cross-channel, or identifier-only authority.",
    "enroll_principal: [PROVENANCE] MUST prove initial installation state by calling `list_principals_by_kind` for the closed owner and operator kinds, or re-authenticate the supplied active owner/operator actor with `load_principal`; then generate collision-resistant principal and credential identities plus a cryptographically random self-identifying bearer `<credential_id>.<secret_material>`. In one UoW transaction it MUST insert one `CabinetPrincipal`, one channel-bound `AccessCredentialRecord` containing only the pepper-protected bearer verifier, and one secret-free `SecurityAuditRecord`, commit, and return the bearer exactly once through `IssuedPrincipalCredential.secret`; rollback MUST expose no bearer and persist no partial row.",
    "provision_capability_grant: [SECURITY_BOUNDARY] MUST open one operation UoW, re-authenticate the active owner/operator grantor and active target with `load_principal`, validate the exact pair against = rules.capability_catalogue.grantable, derive one deterministic complete scope key, and call `load_capability_grant` before conditionally inserting exactly one `CapabilityGrantRecord` plus secret-free audit evidence in the same transaction. Exact replay MUST commit no duplicate and return created false; protected-operator, unknown, affix-confused, cross-channel, inactive, or unauthorized requests MUST roll back without changing grant state.",
    "rotate_credential: [SECURITY_BOUNDARY] MUST open one operation UoW, lock and load the named credential with `lock_credential` and `load_credential`, re-authenticate the command actor with `load_principal`, generate a new collision-resistant credential identity and cryptographically random self-identifying bearer, update the prior `AccessCredentialRecord` to revoked, insert the replacement verifier record and secret-free audit evidence, and commit all changes atomically. It MUST preserve subject identity and channel, return the new bearer exactly once, and never return, retain, or recover the old bearer.",
    "revoke_credential: [BEHAVIOR] MUST open one operation UoW, lock and load only the named credential with `lock_credential` and `load_credential`, verify the command principal binding and active owner/operator actor with `load_principal`, update only that `AccessCredentialRecord`, append secret-free audit evidence, and commit in one transaction. Exact repeated revocation MUST be idempotent; every mismatch or unauthorized request MUST roll back, and later authentication with the revoked bearer MUST fail immediately.",
    "extract_plugin_credential: [SECURITY_BOUNDARY] MUST accept only one well-formed Bearer value on the private plugin route namespace, reject missing, duplicated, oversized, or wrong-scheme headers uniformly, and never log or echo the value.",
    "extract_local_node_credential: [SECURITY_BOUNDARY] MUST accept only one well-formed Bearer value on the synchronization route namespace, reject missing, duplicated, oversized, or wrong-scheme headers uniformly, and keep it distinct from the plugin credential scope.",
    "extract_browser_principal: [SECURITY_BOUNDARY] MUST accept only the TrustedEdge owner assertion injected by the private nginx hop after Basic Auth; reject direct or duplicated assertions, and rely on deployment enforcement that strips the client-supplied header before injection.",
    "resolve_plugin_principal: [SECURITY_BOUNDARY] MUST delegate the single plugin Bearer to `authenticate_request` with exact channel `plugin`, let that operation finish its owned transaction, and accept only when the returned active non-revoked principal has exact kind `owner`. It MUST NOT open another UoW or wrap the transaction-owning authentication call; it MUST reject machine, browser, revoked, absent, or ambiguous identities without an anonymous fallback and raise AuthenticationRequiredError for every failed resolution.",
    "resolve_browser_principal: [SECURITY_BOUNDARY] MUST accept only the exact TrustedEdge label `owner`, open one UoW through `CabinetUnitOfWorkFactory.open`, call `list_principals_by_kind(\"owner\")`, and return an AuthenticatedPrincipal only when exactly one active non-revoked owner exists; every missing, duplicate, inactive, revoked, or other-label result MUST roll back and raise AuthenticationRequiredError. This resolver never validates Basic Auth itself or accepts a public listener.",
    "resolve_local_node_principal: [SECURITY_BOUNDARY] MUST parse the same bounded self-identifying bearer shape as authentication, protect the complete bearer with the configured pepper, open one UoW, and use `load_credential` followed by `load_node` for that credential's exact node subject. It MUST timing-safely verify exact channel `local_node`, require one active non-revoked `local_backend` node supporting the reciprocal contract, commit only secret-free authentication evidence, and raise AuthenticationRequiredError for owner, operator, revoked, incompatible, cross-installation, malformed, or failed credentials.",
    "resolve_capability: [DETERMINISM_OR_ORDERING] MUST match the requested dotted value and channel by exact equality against = rules.capability_catalogue.grantable and exclude every entry in = rules.capability_catalogue.protected_operator, return its single semantic operation in catalogue order, and reject unknown, affix-confused, or cross-channel names without dynamic dispatch.",
    "create_app: [DEPENDENCY_BOUNDARY] MUST preserve the application composition boundary and require all thirteen explicit module services, bind them to private application state, install only the accepted plugin, browser, and sync routers plus empty-body exception mappings, and fail startup when protected configuration or any required service is unavailable.",
    "prepare_chatgpt_proposal: [BEHAVIOR] MUST treat conversational fields as untrusted suggestions, normalize them into the requested typed proposal, preserve missing and uncertain facts, attach exact revision and duplicate warnings, and perform no durable Card, source, effect, or synchronization mutation.",
    "confirm_chatgpt_effect: [SECURITY_BOUNDARY] MUST verify that the owner explicitly confirmed the exact proposal digest, target revision, capability, and effect identity before expiry; any mismatch, ambiguity, decline, or stale revision produces no authorization and no mutation.",
    "report_composite_outcome: [RETURN_SHAPE] MUST return separate typed Card, original-source custody, and local-synchronization outcomes with bounded safe codes, preserving partial or unknown states instead of collapsing them into a single success flag.",
    "begin_effect: [BEHAVIOR] MUST reserve one principal-scoped idempotency identity before mutation, return the prior compatible reservation or committed result on replay, reject conflicting payload reuse, and preserve outcome_unknown for read-only reconciliation.",
    "commit_effect: [PROVENANCE] MUST preserve the effect journal boundary and atomically bind the exact durable operation result and completion time to the existing effect reservation; reject absent, conflicting, or already-differently-committed effects and never rewrite prior evidence.",
    "reconcile_effect: [BEHAVIOR] MUST read the exact reserved effect and its durable result evidence without issuing the mutation again, returning committed, rejected, or outcome_unknown truthfully and leaving all domain state unchanged.",
    "commit_card_revision: [ORCHESTRATION] MUST open and begin one fresh CabinetUnitOfWork, delegate all revision preparation and writes to commit_card_revision_in_unit_of_work, commit only its successful result, and roll back every exception; it MUST NOT duplicate Card canonicalization or expose a committed result before the UoW commits.",
    "prepare_card_revision: [PROVENANCE] MUST validate the supplied canonical Card JSON and declared type, reject every error-severity validation issue, derive the canonical immutable content hash and UTC observation evidence, and return the complete CanonicalCardRevision without reading or mutating persistence.",
    "commit_card_revision_in_unit_of_work: [ORCHESTRATION] MUST require an already active caller-owned CabinetUnitOfWork, lock the exact Card identity, compare the stored current content hash with the command expected_content_hash, call prepare_card_revision, append the immutable revision, and insert or move the current selector; it MUST NOT begin, commit, roll back, or create another UoW.",
    "commit_card_revision_in_unit_of_work: [RETURN_SHAPE] MUST return the exact stored revision with created true and replayed false after a new append, return created false and replayed true only for an identical already-current revision, and otherwise raise the owned validation, not-found, canonical-hash, or revision-conflict error without changing persistence.",
    "search_provider_cards: [DETERMINISM_OR_ORDERING] MUST apply only the closed bounded Provider criteria, encode external text as data, order equal matches by stable Provider Card ID, cap results at the configured search limit, and perform no mutation.",
    "list_project_cards: [DETERMINISM_OR_ORDERING] MUST return authorized canonical Project summaries in the accepted stable ordering with an opaque bounded cursor, never substituting Registry snapshots for Project Card master facts.",
    "get_card_revision: [BEHAVIOR] MUST return only the exact Card ID, type, and content-hash revision requested for package assembly; never silently substitute the current or newer revision and report absence or type mismatch explicitly.",
    "search_invoices: [ORCHESTRATION] MUST open, begin, and finally roll back one CabinetUnitOfWork; call list_current_card_references_by_type with = rules.invoice_workspace.card_type, load every returned reference by its card_id and content_hash, parse each CanonicalCardRevision.canonical_json as InvoiceCardV1, and separately index list_available_working_set_records for = rules.invoice_workspace.working_set_status by revision before building views; it MUST NOT call a mutation.",
    "search_invoices: [DETERMINISM_OR_ORDERING] MUST filter parsed Cards by exact query.status, inclusive issue_date bounds, supplier tax_id for query.provider_id, and casefolded substring query.text over invoice_number and supplier values; order by issue_date descending with missing last, then reference.card_id and reference.content_hash, resume strictly after the item whose content_hash equals query.cursor, and emit at most query.limit items.",
    "search_invoices: [RETURN_SHAPE] MUST construct each InvoiceCardView with the loaded reference, parsed Card, source_status = invoice.source.file_status, and synchronization_status = the matching working-set status or = rules.invoice_workspace.synchronization_unavailable_status; next_cursor is the final emitted content_hash only when more filtered items remain, otherwise None.",
    "get_invoice: [ORCHESTRATION] MUST open, begin, and finally roll back one CabinetUnitOfWork; use load_current_card_reference(invoice_id) only when content_hash is None, then load_card_revision with the resolved card_id and content_hash, parse canonical_json as InvoiceCardV1, require the reference card_type, parsed card_type, and parsed id to match = rules.invoice_workspace and invoice_id, and never substitute another revision.",
    "get_invoice: [RETURN_SHAPE] MUST construct InvoiceCardView from the exact stored reference and parsed Card, set source_status from invoice.source.file_status, and derive synchronization_status only from a list_available_working_set_records result whose revision equals the reference, falling back to = rules.invoice_workspace.synchronization_unavailable_status; any missing or malformed record raises ValidationRejectedError with = rules.invoice_workspace.rejection_codes.not_found.",
    "find_invoice_duplicates: [ORCHESTRATION] MUST open, begin, and finally roll back one CabinetUnitOfWork; call list_current_card_references_by_type with = rules.invoice_workspace.card_type, call load_card_revision for each returned card_id and content_hash, parse its canonical_json as InvoiceCardV1, and read candidate values only through = rules.invoice_duplicate_matching.candidate_field_sources; no stored revision may be synthesized or replaced by its current head.",
    "find_invoice_duplicates: [RULE_REFERENCE] MUST apply all of = rules.invoice_duplicate_matching: normalize strings by strip plus casefold while dates and Decimal values compare exactly, compare only non-null candidate fields, exclude the same invoice id, and construct one InvoiceDuplicateCandidate per revision with invoice_revision = its stored reference and reason_codes in candidate_field_order using reason_code_prefix plus each matched field.",
    "find_invoice_duplicates: [DETERMINISM_OR_ORDERING] MUST return the declared empty tuple when comparable fields are below minimum_match_fields or no revision matches, otherwise sort the constructed candidates by the declared stable_order and never merge, archive, confirm, or select a winner.",
    "prepare_invoice_draft: [ORCHESTRATION] MUST call InvoiceCardV1.model_validate_json on proposal.canonical_json, require the parsed card_type and card_version to equal = rules.invoice_workspace, require proposal.invoice_id when present to equal invoice.id, proposal.currency to equal invoice.currency, and proposal.source_provenance when present to equal invoice.source.origin_context at = rules.invoice_workspace.source_provenance_key; then call validate_invoice exactly once and reuse its duplicate_candidates.",
    "prepare_invoice_draft: [RETURN_SHAPE] MUST construct InvoiceDraftProposal(invoice=validation.normalized_invoice, issues=validation.issues, duplicate_candidates=validation.duplicate_candidates); JSON/model mismatch raises ValidationRejectedError with = rules.invoice_workspace.rejection_codes.validation and no field, identity, actor, source, total, or payment is invented.",
    "validate_invoice: [ORCHESTRATION] MUST evaluate every entry of = rules.invoice_workspace.validation_checks in its declared order against candidate.invoice, including every indexed line, construct a ValidationIssue for each failure with severity/message from = rules.invoice_workspace, the rule code and concrete indexed field_path, expected = rule formula, and actual = the offending value; then construct InvoiceDuplicateCandidateInput from invoice id, invoice_number, supplier.tax_id, issue_date and totals.gross_total and call find_invoice_duplicates exactly once.",
    "validate_invoice: [RETURN_SHAPE] MUST construct InvoiceValidationResult(normalized_invoice=candidate.invoice, issues=the complete tuple sorted by = rules.invoice_workspace.validation_issue_order and line index, duplicate_candidates=the exact duplicate result, revision_context=candidate.expected_revision); it performs no write and never suppresses a failed declared check.",
    "create_invoice_draft: [SECURITY_BOUNDARY] MUST before any write require authorization == command.authorization, authorization.allowed, authorization.capability equal the operation capability in = rules.capability_catalogue.grantable, authorization.principal_id == command.actor.principal_id, and any entity_scope to identify command.draft.invoice.id with no revision; failure raises ValidationRejectedError with = rules.invoice_workspace.rejection_codes.access_denied.",
    "create_invoice_draft: [ORCHESTRATION] MUST require command.draft.invoice.status = rules.invoice_workspace.lifecycle.draft, no issue at = rules.invoice_workspace.validation_issue_severity, and no duplicate_candidates; construct CardRevisionCommitCommand(card_id=invoice.id, card_type=rules.invoice_workspace.card_type, expected_content_hash=None, canonical_json=invoice.model_dump_json(), validation_issues=draft.issues, actor=command.actor) and call commit_card_revision exactly once.",
    "create_invoice_draft: [RETURN_SHAPE] MUST construct InvoiceMutationResult(effect_id=command.effect_id, revision=commit_result.revision, status=commit_result.revision.observed_status, replayed=commit_result.replayed, issues=command.draft.issues, safe_error_code=None); rejection raises the declared validation code and never returns command input as stored evidence.",
    "update_invoice_draft: [SECURITY_BOUNDARY] MUST apply the create authorization checks and additionally require entity_scope.entity_id == command.invoice_id and entity_scope.revision == command.expected_revision; mismatch raises = rules.invoice_workspace.rejection_codes.access_denied before any write.",
    "update_invoice_draft: [ORCHESTRATION] MUST call get_invoice for command.expected_revision, require its invoice id and status = rules.invoice_workspace.lifecycle.draft, require command.proposal.invoice.id equal command.invoice_id and no error-severity issues or duplicates, then construct CardRevisionCommitCommand from proposal.invoice.model_dump_json(), proposal.issues, command.actor and expected_content_hash=command.expected_revision.content_hash and call commit_card_revision once.",
    "update_invoice_draft: [RETURN_SHAPE] MUST construct InvoiceMutationResult from command.effect_id, commit_result.revision, that revision observed_status, commit_result.replayed, proposal.issues and safe_error_code=None; not-found/stale/invalid input raises the declared revision or validation rejection and never returns command.expected_revision as a new result.",
